{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSf9VJ972LMDvTWKvj26hH","type":"tool_result","content":"ok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli\t0.007s\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N17\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":119,\"summary\":\"GitReadError keeps only the first stderr line, which is not the cause when Git warns first. With diff.dirstat=bogus and a corrupt index (bad signature), scope selection reports 'git diff HEAD..worktree failed (revision unknown?): ... exit status 128: warning: Found errors in 'diff.dirstat' config variable:', the check's diff finding and the plain report warning carry only that warning, and the index failure is not marked. An unknown revision loses 'fatal: bad revision' the same way. R2 requires the cause and forbids the revision label; the previous round's commit kept the whole message. Classification also runs on the text after the 300-byte cut. Reproduced with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N18\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":108,\"summary\":\"gitIndexFailureRE misses Git's own index refusals. 'fatal: unknown index entry format 0xff700000' and 'fatal: broken index, expect <hash> in .git/sharedindex.<hash>, got <hash>' are not marked ErrIndexUnreadable, so scope selection labels both '(revision unknown?)' (validate_scope.go:112), which R2 forbids. The previous round's word match marked both. Reproduced on Git 2.56 with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N19\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":309,\"summary\":\"A plain report is still silent, writing '_No files detected_' with no warning, when .git/config is broken or HEAD is invalid: rev-parse --git-dir fails there too. D3 says the report stays silent only where the root is not a repository.\",\"action\":\"Stay silent only on Git's not-a-repository answer for a root with no .git, and warn otherwise.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N20\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":112,\"summary\":\"Every failure not marked as an index failure is still labelled '(revision unknown?)', including a failed index lookup (not a repository, broken config, and by reading an expired lookup deadline), and the message still repeats itself: 'git diff X failed (revision unknown?): git diff failed:'.\",\"action\":\"Add the revision label only when Git rejects the revision, and drop the doubled prefix.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N21\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\",\"line\":536,\"summary\":\"Guards still without a failing test: the ledger passing its context (ReadOnlyIndex there stays green), GitEnglish on the check, hand-over and lookup commands, the report's stderr warning and the memfd write fallback. TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale can only catch a missing English locale where Git's pt_BR translations are installed.\",\"action\":\"Test the ledger deadline and each English-locale site with a Git stand-in, and assert the report warning.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N22\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":312,\"summary\":\"The versioned report still receives the checkout's absolute path, for example when the index cannot be opened ('pose: the index of /abs/root cannot be read: ... open /abs/root/.git/index: permission denied'); those pose-composed errors are not bounded either.\",\"action\":\"Write a root-relative, bounded note into the report and keep the full error on stderr.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay mutation restoring --path-format=absolute leaves the focused pose and cli tests green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the check's command-failure finding now fails TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause; replacing the report warning call (report.go:203 area) leaves the tests green.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N9\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Dropping the report note fails TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, as does removing the outside-repository silence; probes show the note in the report. The broken config or HEAD case is N19.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The ready-transition diff arguments at check.go:1131-1134 are unchanged in this range; pre-existing, open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N12\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"report.go:332 runs git status in English and TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale passes under pt_BR; an overlay probe with a broken .git/config or HEAD still exits silently with '_No files detected_' (N19).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N13\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"A revision named feature/index-rework keeps the revision wording (test at validate_reads_index_test.go:224 passes); the doubled prefix remains on that branch (N20), and the narrower match introduced N18.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N14\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Probe outside a repository and with a broken config or HEAD: the lookup error carries Git's fatal line and is not ErrIndexUnreadable (git_worktree_reads.go:52-60); TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause passes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N15\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"The note is one line and Git's message is cut at 300 bytes (git_worktree_reads.go:119-124, report.go:312); probes still show absolute checkout paths in the report (N22).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N16\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Mutations of the lookup context, report-side English locale, hand-over mark, silence and note now fail a test; the ledger context, three English-locale sites and memfd write stay green (N21).\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"Read the round 3 diff (d93acdc2..f9c29770) and its callers; ran the focused cli and pose tests twice under -race and go vet; probed by overlay on Git 2.56: reordered entries, unknown entry format, a config warning ahead of a corrupt index and of a bad revision, broken and missing shared index, bad signature, broken config and HEAD, unreadable index and non-repository; mutated the guards for context, locale, hand-over, fallbacks, report silence, note and warning, check finding, path format and index protection; ran the planned pose tools and both validate commands.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N18\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N18\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-git-spawns-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N17\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-profile-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined signatures and callers: GitEnglish is an addition, ReadOnlyIndex keeps its signature, report keeps exit 0 and no MCP schema or record format changes. Error wording changes are covered by the findings.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N17\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-4d3175efde4220c5\",\"rationale\":\"D2 removes the stat-then-open race and keeps FIFOs from blocking; D1 and L1 rest on measured Git behaviour; D3 addresses the deadline and locale causes. Its first-line bound and message list do not fully serve R2, recorded as N17 and N18. The sealed design assessment lists no structural deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N19\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N17\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N18\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/artifact-claim-boundary-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The 13 implementation files are the ones the spec lists, artifact-check strict exits 0, and round 3 stays within R2 and D3.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the open and hand-over paths: non-blocking open judged by fstat, 512 MiB bound, sanitised Git environment, 0600 private copy removed after use. Git text kept in errors is now bounded; local paths in the report are noted as low in N22.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"One regexp, one locale helper and one report helper are small and used. Classifying by an enumerated first line is invalid once Git warns first or refuses the index in other words (N17, N18); choosing the fatal line and treating a failure as a revision one only when Git rejects the revision would be as small.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-read-only-index-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-4d3175efde4220c5\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Three HTTP consumer gaps reported, on endpoints this range does not touch.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the recorded attestation.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun in the sandbox: exit 1, 236 steps, 224 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. The failed tests match sandbox limits (directory ownership by another user, denied network and delegation, runtime tests failing to start or timing out) or sit in files this range does not touch. Focused subject tests pass under -race. Relies on the sealed evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun in the sandbox: exit 1, 233 steps, 221 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. The failed tests match sandbox limits (directory ownership by another user, denied network and delegation, runtime tests failing to start or timing out) or sit in files this range does not touch. Focused subject tests pass under -race. Relies on the sealed evidence.\"}\n ]\n}\n```\nDraft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"b8d136a3-f043-420c-895b-081d201efce6","timestamp":"2026-11-27T02:53:59.863Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli\t0.007s\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N17\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":119,\"summary\":\"GitReadError keeps only the first stderr line, which is not the cause when Git warns first. With diff.dirstat=bogus and a corrupt index (bad signature), scope selection reports 'git diff HEAD..worktree failed (revision unknown?): ... exit status 128: warning: Found errors in 'diff.dirstat' config variable:', the check's diff finding and the plain report warning carry only that warning, and the index failure is not marked. An unknown revision loses 'fatal: bad revision' the same way. R2 requires the cause and forbids the revision label; the previous round's commit kept the whole message. Classification also runs on the text after the 300-byte cut. Reproduced with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N18\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":108,\"summary\":\"gitIndexFailureRE misses Git's own index refusals. 'fatal: unknown index entry format 0xff700000' and 'fatal: broken index, expect <hash> in .git/sharedindex.<hash>, got <hash>' are not marked ErrIndexUnreadable, so scope selection labels both '(revision unknown?)' (validate_scope.go:112), which R2 forbids. The previous round's word match marked both. Reproduced on Git 2.56 with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N19\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":309,\"summary\":\"A plain report is still silent, writing '_No files detected_' with no warning, when .git/config is broken or HEAD is invalid: rev-parse --git-dir fails there too. D3 says the report stays silent only where the root is not a repository.\",\"action\":\"Stay silent only on Git's not-a-repository answer for a root with no .git, and warn otherwise.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N20\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":112,\"summary\":\"Every failure not marked as an index failure is still labelled '(revision unknown?)', including a failed index lookup (not a repository, broken config, and by reading an expired lookup deadline), and the message still repeats itself: 'git diff X failed (revision unknown?): git diff failed:'.\",\"action\":\"Add the revision label only when Git rejects the revision, and drop the doubled prefix.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N21\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\",\"line\":536,\"summary\":\"Guards still without a failing test: the ledger passing its context (ReadOnlyIndex there stays green), GitEnglish on the check, hand-over and lookup commands, the report's stderr warning and the memfd write fallback. TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale can only catch a missing English locale where Git's pt_BR translations are installed.\",\"action\":\"Test the ledger deadline and each English-locale site with a Git stand-in, and assert the report warning.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N22\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":312,\"summary\":\"The versioned report still receives the checkout's absolute path, for example when the index cannot be opened ('pose: the index of /abs/root cannot be read: ... open /abs/root/.git/index: permission denied'); those pose-composed errors are not bounded either.\",\"action\":\"Write a root-relative, bounded note into the report and keep the full error on stderr.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay mutation restoring --path-format=absolute leaves the focused pose and cli tests green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the check's command-failure finding now fails TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause; replacing the report warning call (report.go:203 area) leaves the tests green.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N9\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Dropping the report note fails TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, as does removing the outside-repository silence; probes show the note in the report. The broken config or HEAD case is N19.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The ready-transition diff arguments at check.go:1131-1134 are unchanged in this range; pre-existing, open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N12\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"report.go:332 runs git status in English and TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale passes under pt_BR; an overlay probe with a broken .git/config or HEAD still exits silently with '_No files detected_' (N19).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N13\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"A revision named feature/index-rework keeps the revision wording (test at validate_reads_index_test.go:224 passes); the doubled prefix remains on that branch (N20), and the narrower match introduced N18.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N14\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Probe outside a repository and with a broken config or HEAD: the lookup error carries Git's fatal line and is not ErrIndexUnreadable (git_worktree_reads.go:52-60); TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause passes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N15\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"The note is one line and Git's message is cut at 300 bytes (git_worktree_reads.go:119-124, report.go:312); probes still show absolute checkout paths in the report (N22).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N16\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Mutations of the lookup context, report-side English locale, hand-over mark, silence and note now fail a test; the ledger context, three English-locale sites and memfd write stay green (N21).\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"Read the round 3 diff (d93acdc2..f9c29770) and its callers; ran the focused cli and pose tests twice under -race and go vet; probed by overlay on Git 2.56: reordered entries, unknown entry format, a config warning ahead of a corrupt index and of a bad revision, broken and missing shared index, bad signature, broken config and HEAD, unreadable index and non-repository; mutated the guards for context, locale, hand-over, fallbacks, report silence, note and warning, check finding, path format and index protection; ran the planned pose tools and both validate commands.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N18\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N18\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-git-spawns-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N17\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-profile-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined signatures and callers: GitEnglish is an addition, ReadOnlyIndex keeps its signature, report keeps exit 0 and no MCP schema or record format changes. Error wording changes are covered by the findings.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N17\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-4d3175efde4220c5\",\"rationale\":\"D2 removes the stat-then-open race and keeps FIFOs from blocking; D1 and L1 rest on measured Git behaviour; D3 addresses the deadline and locale causes. Its first-line bound and message list do not fully serve R2, recorded as N17 and N18. The sealed design assessment lists no structural deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N19\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N17\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N18\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/artifact-claim-boundary-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The 13 implementation files are the ones the spec lists, artifact-check strict exits 0, and round 3 stays within R2 and D3.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the open and hand-over paths: non-blocking open judged by fstat, 512 MiB bound, sanitised Git environment, 0600 private copy removed after use. Git text kept in errors is now bounded; local paths in the report are noted as low in N22.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"One regexp, one locale helper and one report helper are small and used. Classifying by an enumerated first line is invalid once Git warns first or refuses the index in other words (N17, N18); choosing the fatal line and treating a failure as a revision one only when Git rejects the revision would be as small.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-read-only-index-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-4d3175efde4220c5\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Three HTTP consumer gaps reported, on endpoints this range does not touch.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the recorded attestation.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun in the sandbox: exit 1, 236 steps, 224 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. The failed tests match sandbox limits (directory ownership by another user, denied network and delegation, runtime tests failing to start or timing out) or sit in files this range does not touch. Focused subject tests pass under -race. Relies on the sealed evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun in the sandbox: exit 1, 233 steps, 221 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. The failed tests match sandbox limits (directory ownership by another user, denied network and delegation, runtime tests failing to start or timing out) or sit in files this range does not touch. Focused subject tests pass under -race. Relies on the sealed evidence.\"}\n ]\n}\n```\nDraft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TSf9VJ972LMDvTWKvj26hH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
